1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,310
A bundle lists products, and each bundle has someone who manages it.

2
00:00:05,310 --> 00:00:10,494
The Content Picker and User Picker fields store those links as choices from a list.

3
00:00:10,494 --> 00:00:14,920
In this video, you add both fields to a content type and fill them in.

4
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:22,989
Orchard Core connects content items in several ways.

5
00:00:22,989 --> 00:00:27,355
A Bag Part stores items inside their parent, a List Part keeps them

6
00:00:27,355 --> 00:00:31,900
in a container like a blog, and Taxonomies tag them with shared terms.

7
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:35,141
A Content Picker Field is different:

8
00:00:35,141 --> 00:00:38,107
the editor chooses items that already exist.

9
00:00:38,107 --> 00:00:42,201
The field keeps a reference to each chosen item, not a copy, so

10
00:00:42,201 --> 00:00:44,870
one product can appear in many bundles.

11
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:48,092
A product bundle can pick its products.

12
00:00:48,092 --> 00:00:51,444
A blog post can pick related posts for further reading.

13
00:00:51,444 --> 00:00:55,290
And any content item can pick the user accounts connected to it.

14
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:59,394
The Content Fields module provides three picker fields:

15
00:00:59,394 --> 00:01:03,902
the Content Picker Field for content items, the User Picker Field for users,

16
00:01:03,902 --> 00:01:08,521
and the Localization Set Content Picker Field for the translations of an item.

17
00:01:08,521 --> 00:01:11,710
The last one needs the Content Localization feature.

18
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:20,546
Let's relate the Product Bundle content type to the Product content type.

19
00:01:20,546 --> 00:01:26,230
Under Design, Content Definition, Content Types, we edit Product Bundle and select Add Field.

20
00:01:26,684 --> 00:01:28,703
The Display Name is Products.

21
00:01:28,703 --> 00:01:33,375
For Field Type, we choose Content Picker Field, and select Save & Configure

22
00:01:33,375 --> 00:01:35,394
to open the field's settings.

23
00:01:35,870 --> 00:01:39,366
Required means an editor must pick at least one item.

24
00:01:39,366 --> 00:01:42,269
Allow multiple lets an editor pick several.

25
00:01:42,269 --> 00:01:46,120
A bundle holds many products, so we turn on Allow multiple.

26
00:01:46,581 --> 00:01:49,946
Contained Content Types sets what the picker offers.

27
00:01:49,946 --> 00:01:55,343
Display All Content Types offers every type without a stereotype, and Stereotype offers

28
00:01:55,343 --> 00:01:58,651
the types that share a stereotype, such as widgets.

29
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:01,915
Content Types offers only the types you tick.

30
00:02:01,915 --> 00:02:04,658
A bundle picks products, so we tick Product.

31
00:02:05,114 --> 00:02:08,956
Hint adds a line of help below the field in the content editor.

32
00:02:08,956 --> 00:02:14,134
We write one, save the settings, and the type lists Products as a Content Picker Field.

33
00:02:18,364 --> 00:02:22,794
In the list of Product Bundle items, let's edit the Weekend Camping Bundle.

34
00:02:22,794 --> 00:02:26,404
Its editor shows the Products field, with the hint we wrote.

35
00:02:26,869 --> 00:02:31,176
Typing in the field searches the content items of the allowed types.

36
00:02:31,176 --> 00:02:35,890
The picker matches the typed text anywhere in a title or content type name.

37
00:02:35,890 --> 00:02:38,509
We type pack and select Trail Backpack.

38
00:02:38,974 --> 00:02:43,150
Because Allow multiple is on, we add more products the same way:

39
00:02:43,150 --> 00:02:45,059
Camp Stove, then Headlamp.

40
00:02:45,059 --> 00:02:47,564
All three choices stay in the field.

41
00:02:48,018 --> 00:02:52,888
We select Publish, and the bundle is saved together with its three products.

42
00:02:53,347 --> 00:02:55,112
We open the bundle's page.

43
00:02:55,112 --> 00:02:59,967
The Products field lists each chosen product as a link to that product's own page.

44
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:04,894
Following the Camp Stove link opens that product's page, which is a content

45
00:03:04,894 --> 00:03:06,110
item of its own.

46
00:03:10,364 --> 00:03:14,476
To record who manages a bundle, we select Add Field on the Product

47
00:03:14,476 --> 00:03:18,644
Bundle type again and add a User Picker Field named Bundle Manager.

48
00:03:18,644 --> 00:03:22,584
This field type is available when the Users feature is enabled.

49
00:03:23,061 --> 00:03:26,722
The settings repeat Required and Allow multiple.

50
00:03:26,722 --> 00:03:30,451
Under Roles, Display All Users offers every user.

51
00:03:30,451 --> 00:03:36,281
We clear it and tick Editor, so the picker offers only users in the Editor role.

52
00:03:36,743 --> 00:03:40,286
The display mode decides how the field appears on the page.

53
00:03:40,286 --> 00:03:44,210
Standard looks up each user when the page is shown, and User Names

54
00:03:44,210 --> 00:03:48,079
shows the names saved with the bundle the last time it was saved.

55
00:03:48,079 --> 00:03:49,823
We keep Standard and save.

56
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:54,514
In the bundle's editor, we type the letters o r.

57
00:03:54,514 --> 00:03:58,946
The user names jordan, morgan and taylor all contain them, but only jordan

58
00:03:58,946 --> 00:04:02,269
and morgan are editors, so the picker lists those two.

59
00:04:02,269 --> 00:04:03,543
We select jordan.

60
00:04:03,999 --> 00:04:06,571
We publish the bundle and open its page.

61
00:04:06,571 --> 00:04:09,759
It shows Bundle Manager, followed by the user name.

62
00:04:13,959 --> 00:04:17,364
By default, the picker searches the database by title.

63
00:04:17,364 --> 00:04:20,769
Two optional features add another editor to the field:

64
00:04:20,769 --> 00:04:27,125
Lucene Content Picker adds a Lucene editor, and Elasticsearch Content Picker adds an Elasticsearch editor.

65
00:04:27,125 --> 00:04:29,339
Each comes with an Index setting.

66
00:04:31,005 --> 00:04:34,995
With the Lucene Content Picker feature enabled, we open the settings of the

67
00:04:34,995 --> 00:04:38,986
Products field and choose Lucene in the drop-down list labeled What type of

68
00:04:38,986 --> 00:04:40,365
editor should be used?

69
00:04:40,895 --> 00:04:46,950
The Index setting lists the Lucene indexes of the site, which you create under Search, Indexes.

70
00:04:46,950 --> 00:04:51,567
The index must contain the content types the field offers, so we select

71
00:04:51,567 --> 00:04:54,865
Catalog, an index of the Product items, and save.

72
00:04:56,449 --> 00:04:59,011
In the bundle's editor, we type rain.

73
00:04:59,011 --> 00:05:03,719
The Lucene editor matches the start of a title, so Rain Jacket is listed.

74
00:05:04,175 --> 00:05:08,135
Typing jacket finds nothing, because no title starts with it.

75
00:05:12,335 --> 00:05:17,119
A Content Picker Field relates an item to other items, and Contained Content

76
00:05:17,119 --> 00:05:19,394
Types sets which types it offers.

77
00:05:19,394 --> 00:05:23,478
A User Picker Field relates an item to users, and can offer only

78
00:05:23,478 --> 00:05:25,345
the users in chosen roles.

79
00:05:26,095 --> 00:05:31,155
Both store a reference to each choice, and both allow one choice or several.

80
00:05:31,155 --> 00:05:36,585
The Lucene and Elasticsearch editors change where a Content Picker Field searches.

81
00:05:38,585 --> 00:05:44,183
Content Picker and User Picker fields let editors relate content by choosing from a list.

82
00:05:44,183 --> 00:05:45,715
Thanks for watching.

